## How to revise

Revise the method body so it verifies. Read the error message for which
obligation failed (precondition, invariant, or postcondition) and at which
line, then adjust either the tracked state or the loop invariants so that
obligation becomes provable — this is often a smaller, more targeted fix than
rewriting the whole strategy.

Common Dafny pitfalls to check:
- Methods cannot be called directly inside expression contexts.
  Call the method first, bind its result to a local variable, then use that
  variable in the condition.
- A loop invariant must be re-established by every branch of the loop body,
  including early-exit branches — an invariant that holds on entry but is
  broken by one rarely-taken branch will still fail verification.
- A helper's precondition must be provable from the state you are tracking at
  the exact point you call it, not just true "in general" across the strategy.

